From 332ffaaa36746c33d7eaffd81e72b523f20c821e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kara Zajac <kara@soulstone.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:43:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] maki: a control port for tests, and a profile of what the CPU
 runs

With --usb PORT, PORT+3 takes a test's commands, a line each, and answers each:
- `press N [D]`: button N, for D instructions (20M if not given); `press 3+4` presses those
  together (maki's menu chord).
- `shot NAME`: the screen now, into OUT/NAME.pgm.
- `screen`: the screen now, as text.
- `profile L S`: from now, for L instructions, every S, which process runs (satp's ASID, which
  Xous makes the PID), in which mode, whether the CPU waits, and where: OUT/profile-*.txt.
- `quit`: stop, as if the last checkpoint had come (the summary, --flash-out, --show-owc).

A test can then install an app over the USB pipe, open it, look at it and close it again, and
see where a slow launch's time goes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
